    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3670",
      "problem": "The graph below shows the function $y=\\csc{\\left(2x\\right)}+D,$ where $D$ is a constant. What is the value of $D?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14257592/assets/d4c9f866923348641a68a0462948e31d2ea59a5729775c2ae3d38f362c7ad5cd.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The constant $D$ represents a vertical shift of the function $y=\\csc\\left(2x\\right).$\n\nSince the local minimum of cosecant is $y=1,$ from the graph we see that the given curve is shifted **down** by $1$ unit. So, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\csc\\left(2x\\right)-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $D =-1.$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14257592/observations/step-e3670-644d6e3b1052acfeccca.html",
